    "text": "<p>Let us consider <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, a constant function, as constant functions are continuous and differentiable everywhere.</p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>c</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>",
